  "location": "2.1 and 4.2",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "acamprosate calcium: 2.1 and 4.2 give different instructions for one patient",
      "summary": "2.1 reads “creatinine clearance of 30 to 50 mL/min”. 4.2 reads “creatinine clearance of ≤30 mL/min”. Example: At creatinine clearance exactly 30 mL/min the label gives a reduced dose (2.1, 5.1, 12.3) and a contraindication (4.2, 8.6, Highlights). The same text is in 8 labels from 8 labelers in the DailyMed release of 29 October 2026.",
      "impact": "Potential effect on a prescribing decision: low; careful reading of the whole label usually resolves it. Arxo does not say which instruction is correct and gives no dose."
    }
  },
